      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Design the tool contract: input = { configId, optional filter params }; it resolves the surface's existing saved-query/FetchXML by configId (reuse the DEFINITION, not model SQL).</step>
    <step order="2">Execute the resolved query server-side over OBO via the existing query-execution path (DataverseUserClient / read_query internals) — inject `today` deterministically.</step>
    <step order="3">Compute derived predicates server-side (overdue = dueDate &lt; today; counts) and return grid-shaped rows carrying record ids for citation.</step>
    <step order="4">Register the tool as an ADR-039 catalog row consuming the Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ facade — no fork of internals.</step>
    <step order="5">Add/extend unit tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (correct count, today injected, no model-SQL path, record-id citations present).</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build + dotnet publish size check; record absolute size + delta; run the vulnerable-package scan.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If reusing an existing saved-query/FetchXML by configId cannot express a needed overview predicate without either model-authored SQL or a new per-grid handler, STOP and escalate (§11 reuse-first + ADR-039 catalog bound) rather than adding N handlers or accepting model SQL.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>`read_query` (generic) rejects GETDATE()/COUNT/aggregates — the exact R2 UAT defect. No parameterized configId overview tool exists.</existing>
    <extension>Extends existing query execution (wraps a saved-query + injects today) — ONE parameterized tool, not N per-grid handlers.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>"How many overdue tasks do I have?" fails (model authors unsupported SQL → query error, duplicate tab); the overview DoD cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/** (parameterized overview tool handler)</output>
    <output type="code">the ADR-039 catalog row registering the tool</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ overview-tool unit tests</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">"How many overdue tasks do I have?" answers the correct count (overdue computed server-side with today injected, reusing the My Tasks saved-query).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The answer opens/directs to the Tasks tab with NO duplicate tab.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NO query error is produced (no model-authored GETDATE()/aggregate SQL).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The tool does NOT ask the user for the date (today injected server-side).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Returned rows carry record-id citations; no item content enters the prompt (ADR-015).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The tool reuses the surface's existing saved-query definition by configId — no per-grid handler, no model-authored SQL (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size ≤60 MB reported (absolute + delta); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Unit tests added/updated in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ and pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Contrast with the generic `read_query`, which rejects GETDATE()/COUNT/aggregates (the R2 UAT defect this task closes). Task 021 wires this same tool across all grids + Briefing + Calendar via configId — keep the contract surface-agnostic. Coordinate with redesign-r2 on the PublicContracts seam; /conflict-check before the PR.</notes>
